"recognitionPrompt" = "Read the music festival timetable in the images I attached. Reply with a single JSON object only: no explanation, no heading, no Markdown code block.\n\nFormat (keep the field names as they are):\n{\"version\":1,\"timeZone\":null,\"days\":[{\"date\":\"2026-10-17\",\"stages\":[{\"name\":\"STAGE\",\"performances\":[{\"artist\":\"ARTIST\",\"start\":\"18:00\",\"end\":\"19:00\"}]}]}]}\n\nRules:\n1. Extract every performance shown: date, stage, artist, start time and end time.\n2. Copy artist and stage names exactly as printed. Do not translate, romanize or correct them.\n3. Group by date, then by stage, keeping the order shown in the images.\n4. Use 24-hour HH:mm. Sets after midnight that belong to the previous day's schedule stay under that day, with the time as printed (e.g. \"00:30\").\n5. Write dates as YYYY-MM-DD; if the year is not shown, write MM-DD.\n6. Use null for any value you cannot read with certainty. Never guess.\n7. Do not add performances that are not in the images.\n8. Fill timeZone with an IANA identifier (e.g. \"Europe/London\") only if the images state it; otherwise null.\n9. If there are several images, merge them into one JSON object.";
